{
 "schema": "os-optics-kit.optimize-spec",
 "schema_version": 1,
 "description": "Refine the five-element F/3.5 aspheric lens for RMS spot size at every field (0, 12.5, 25 deg) and wavelength (F, d, C): free the L1 front radius, the L5 back radius, the L5 front fourth-order term, the L2 front conic and the image-plane position, each within a local range around the start. Held: the focal length at 50 +- 0.25 mm (paraxial EFL at 587.56 nm), the glass at least 3 mm thick (optical-solid check) and the working aperture: the stop opening is not a variable, every pupil ray arrives on axis and at 12.5 deg, and at least 75 % at 25 deg (the start: 96, 89 and 86 of 96 at F, d, C). The spot RMS counts arriving rays only, so these rays constraints keep the search from shrinking spots by vignetting; ray_loss is report because the start already loses rays at 25 deg. The best design is re-checked with twice the pupil rings.",
